    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d870">

                <pb facs="1031" n="1015" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg1015"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.516 Export Import Bank/10–1347:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in Peru
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-30T17:00:00-05:00">October 30, 1947—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>549. Urtels 733 Oct 10, 738 Oct 13.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d870-f1"/> Maffry
                    Eximbank Oct 29 informed Peru Commercial Counselor by letter that “Board
                    Directors has given new consideration to matter (reference Bank’s letter Sep
                        23<anchor n="29" xml:id="d870-f2"/>) and has reviewed with Dept
                    conversations held with Formin in July regarding offer settlement made by Peru
                    Govt to holders its defaulted obligations. Dept has informed Bank that these
                    conversations removed obstacle which had heretofore stood in way consideration
                    by Bank of Peru loan applications. Accordingly Bank is prepared consider
                    proposals for financing projects in Peru on their individual merits”.</p>
                <p>You may inform Peru Govt.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d870-f1" n="28" xml:id="d870-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d870-f2" n="29" xml:id="d870-f2-content">
                <p>Letter from the Export-Import Bank to the Peruvian Commercial Counselor, referred
                    to in the Ambassador’s telegram 733, October 10, <ref target="#pg1013">p.
                        1013</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
